Helios DXVK fork: dynamic-buffer discards from the local allocation cache when there is no host-visible VRAM

Conduit guest/windows. Applied after 0020 by ci/windows/Build-Driver.ps1.

Each D3D11 context keeps a local allocation cache for the discard slices of
dynamic buffers (Map WRITE_DISCARD). It is created for DEVICE_LOCAL |
HOST_VISIBLE | HOST_COHERENT memory. NVK over RM exposes no such type by
default (its BAR heap is off, NVK_RM_BAR_MB=0), so the cache had no memory
type and createBufferResource skipped it on every discard: it called
allocateMemory with DEVICE_LOCAL (no type; returned null under the
allocator's global lock), then again without DEVICE_LOCAL, which
suballocated from the system-memory mapped pool and created a new
DxvkResourceAllocation, and the freed slice later took the same lock to go
back. In CS2 that path was most of the render thread's time under
D3D11ImmediateContext::Map.

- d3d11: the existing fallback that recreates an unusable cache without
  DEVICE_LOCAL is off in this A/B build (HELIOS_DXVK_LOCAL_ALLOC_CACHE_FALLBACK=1
  turns it on). It changes nothing on a device that has host-visible VRAM;
  without one, the slices land in the same HOST_VISIBLE system memory as
  before, now from the cache (no allocator lock, slices recycled as-is
  through the shared cache). The immediate context logs once which memory
  the cache uses.
- dxvk: allocateMemory returns before taking the allocator lock when no
  memory type matches the request (the types and heaps are fixed at device
  creation), so the remaining DEVICE_LOCAL-first attempts (discard slices
  larger than the cache's 128 KiB limit) cost no lock.

diff --git a/src/d3d11/d3d11_context.cpp b/src/d3d11/d3d11_context.cpp
index 5d4638b6..133e34d1 100644
--- a/src/d3d11/d3d11_context.cpp
+++ b/src/d3d11/d3d11_context.cpp
@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@
 #include <algorithm>
+#include <atomic>
 
 #include "../dxvk/dxvk_helios_producer.h"
 
@@ -52,11 +53,24 @@ namespace dxvk {
 
     m_allocationCache = m_device->createAllocationCache(bufferUsage, memoryFlags);
 
-    if (heliosLocalAllocCacheFallback() && !m_allocationCache.isUsable()) {
+    const bool heliosCacheHadType = m_allocationCache.isUsable();
+
+    if (heliosLocalAllocCacheFallback() && !heliosCacheHadType) {
       m_allocationCache = m_device->createAllocationCache(bufferUsage,
         memoryFlags & ~VK_MEMORY_PROPERTY_DEVICE_LOCAL_BIT);
     }
 
+    if (!IsDeferred) {
+      static std::atomic<bool> s_heliosCacheLogged = { false };
+
+      if (!s_heliosCacheLogged.exchange(true)) {
+        Logger::info(str::format("Helios: D3D11 local allocation cache ",
+          heliosCacheHadType ? "in host-visible VRAM"
+            : m_allocationCache.isUsable() ? "in host-visible system memory (no host-visible VRAM type)"
+            : "unusable (no host-visible VRAM type; HELIOS_DXVK_LOCAL_ALLOC_CACHE_FALLBACK=0)"));
+      }
+    }
+
     if (!IsDeferred) {
       m_heliosFrontendCache = m_device->createAllocationCache(bufferUsage, memoryFlags);
 
diff --git a/src/d3d11/d3d11_context.h b/src/d3d11/d3d11_context.h
index b61cdef5..d19f4c88 100644
--- a/src/d3d11/d3d11_context.h
+++ b/src/d3d11/d3d11_context.h
@@ -158,17 +158,25 @@ namespace dxvk {
   }
 
   /**
-   * \brief Helios D3D11 local-allocation-cache fallback experiment
+   * \brief Helios D3D11 local allocation cache without host-visible VRAM
    *
-   * Default OFF. `HELIOS_DXVK_LOCAL_ALLOC_CACHE_FALLBACK=1` retries only an
-   * unusable D3D11 local cache without DEVICE_LOCAL in its cache request.
-   * The cache is selected once per process; buffer allocation properties and
-   * the allocator's normal per-allocation fallback remain unchanged.
+   * Default OFF (A/B build). The context's local allocation cache serves the discard
+   * slices of dynamic buffers (Map WRITE_DISCARD) and asks for
+   * DEVICE_LOCAL | HOST_VISIBLE | HOST_COHERENT memory. A device without such
+   * a memory type (NVK on RM without its BAR heap, a GPU without a BAR
+   * window) leaves that cache with no memory type, so every discard went to
+   * the allocator: a failed DEVICE_LOCAL attempt, then a suballocation from
+   * the system-memory mapped pool and a new allocation object, both under
+   * the allocator's global lock, and the same lock again when the slice is
+   * freed. Those slices land in HOST_VISIBLE system memory either way (the
+   * allocator drops DEVICE_LOCAL when no type has it), so the cache is then
+   * created for that memory instead and discards are served from it.
+   * `HELIOS_DXVK_LOCAL_ALLOC_CACHE_FALLBACK=1` turns it on.
    */
   inline bool heliosLocalAllocCacheFallback() {
     static const bool enabled = [] {
       const char* env = std::getenv("HELIOS_DXVK_LOCAL_ALLOC_CACHE_FALLBACK");
       return env && env[0] == '1' && env[1] == '\0';
     }();
     return enabled;
   }
diff --git a/src/dxvk/dxvk_memory.cpp b/src/dxvk/dxvk_memory.cpp
index bee66cbd..e55c9a89 100644
--- a/src/dxvk/dxvk_memory.cpp
+++ b/src/dxvk/dxvk_memory.cpp
@@ -832,8 +832,6 @@ namespace dxvk {
   Rc<DxvkResourceAllocation> DxvkMemoryAllocator::allocateMemory(
     const VkMemoryRequirements&             requirements,
     const DxvkAllocationInfo&               allocationInfo) {
-    std::lock_guard<dxvk::mutex> lock(m_mutex);
-
     // If we're allocating device-local memory, only consider memory types from
     // the first reported heap. This way, we avoid falling back to HVV on systems
     // without resizeable BAR by accident.
@@ -842,6 +840,15 @@ namespace dxvk {
     if (memoryTypeMask && (allocationInfo.properties & VK_MEMORY_PROPERTY_DEVICE_LOCAL_BIT))
       memoryTypeMask &= m_memTypes[bit::tzcnt(memoryTypeMask)].heap->memoryTypes;
 
+    // Helios: memory types and heaps are fixed at device creation, so a request
+    // no type can satisfy (DEVICE_LOCAL | HOST_VISIBLE on a device without
+    // host-visible VRAM, which callers then retry without DEVICE_LOCAL) fails
+    // here without taking the allocator lock.
+    if (!memoryTypeMask)
+      return nullptr;
+
+    std::lock_guard<dxvk::mutex> lock(m_mutex);
+
     // Ensure the allocation size is also aligned
     VkDeviceSize size = align(requirements.size, requirements.alignment);
 
